WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
Second contribution exercise, this time on the UI layer.

2
00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:07.000
We take a small component you already know from the sidebar — the notification bell — and extend it with one small, real, end-to-end feature.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.734
NotificationBell.

4
00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:15.460
tsx is deliberately small — a button with an unread badge, and a dropdown listing history from useToast, its own little Zustand store, same one-object-plus-actions shape as store.

5
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.000
ts from E66 but scoped to just toasts: history, unread, clearUnread, clearHistory.

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.340
The feature: let a viewer mute one kind of notification — say, info toasts, which fire the most and matter least — without touching success or error.

7
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:29.000
Small, real, and it needs a setting that survives a restart, not just component state.

8
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.542
That's why this hooks into the real store.

9
00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:31.056
ts, not toast.

10
00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:34.729
ts's local one — a mute preference belongs alongside every other durable setting, saved to settings.

11
00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:35.757
json like everything in E44.

12
00:00:35.757 --> 00:00:42.000
Add a field to the settings shape, mutedToastKinds, and use the store's existing update action to change it — the same pattern any settings panel in the app already uses.

13
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.281
toast.

14
00:00:42.281 --> 00:00:53.270
ts's push function is where every notification is born, so that's where muting has to be enforced: read the current mutedToastKinds from the main store, and if this kind is in it, skip appending to history and skip incrementing unread.

15
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.000
One conditional, right at the source.

16
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:02.102
Last piece: a control inside the bell's own dropdown, next to Clear — a small toggle per kind, calling updateSettings straight from the component, exactly the way ChatWindow.

17
00:01:02.102 --> 00:01:03.408
tsx called store actions in E66.

18
00:01:03.408 --> 00:01:07.000
No new panel, no new route — the feature lives entirely inside the component it extends.

19
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:14.797
Verify end to end: mute info, trigger something that would normally toast info, confirm silence — then restart the app entirely and confirm the mute survived, because it's in settings.

20
00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:17.000
json now, not component state that resets on reload.

21
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.612
One episode left in the entire series.

22
00:01:18.612 --> 00:01:24.000
We close the developer track, and the course, by looking at where this project has actually been and where it's actually going.

